# .semgrepignore - Semgrep (Layer 2) scan-exclusion list
# Syntax: gitignore-style glob patterns
# (https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore#_pattern_format).
#
# Scope: excludes vendored dependencies and build / cache / test output so the
# Semgrep scan (results-semgrep.sarif) reports on first-party code only. Known
# CVEs in dependencies are covered separately by OSV-Scanner (Layer 4) against
# yarn.lock, not by Semgrep.
#
# First-party scan targets are intentionally NOT excluded here:
#   apps/**, packages/** (TS/JS source), .github/** (CI workflows + actions),
#   Dockerfile, docker-compose*.yml, .env.example, .env.appStore.example.

# Vendored dependencies (npm / Yarn Berry)
node_modules
.yarn

# Build / compiled output
.next
dist
build
out

# Tooling caches
.turbo

# Test / coverage output
coverage

# Minified / generated assets
*.min.js
